
<% content_for :title, "Perspectives on Addiction | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="bipolar-perspectives-page addiction-perspectives-index">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="bipolar-perspectives-hero">

    <div class="bipolar-perspectives-hero-content">

      <p class="bipolar-perspectives-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / ADDICTION / PERSPECTIVES
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>ANOTHER</span>
        <span>WAY TO</span>
        <span>LOOK AT IT.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="bipolar-perspectives-intro">
        MORE THAN ONE STORY.<br>
        DIFFERENT LENSES.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- STORIES / CONTEXT -->
  <section class="bipolar-perspectives-topics"
           id="addiction-stories">

    <div class="bipolar-perspectives-heading">

      <p>START WITH THE STORIES</p>

      <h2>
        BEFORE<br>
        THE LENSES.
      </h2>

      <p class="bipolar-perspectives-subtitle">
        Three stories. Three sets of decisions and real, deserved consequences.
        Read what happened, then look at each experience through
        nine different perspectives. Same facts, different questions,
        and no pretending the consequences didn't happen. You committed the sins; 
        you are responsible for your actions.
      </p>

    </div>

    <div class="bipolar-perspectives-grid">

      <!-- FIRST DUI -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_first_dui_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-yellow" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">01 / THE STORY</p>

        <h3>
          FIRST<br>
          DUI
        </h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          Your back is killing you. Sciatica has taken over
          your life, and alcohol looks like a quick solution.
          You stop at the liquor store, drink while driving,
          and turn a search for pain relief into your first DUI.
        </p>

        <span>READ WHAT HAPPENED →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- THIRD DUI -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_third_dui_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-pink" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">02 / THE STORY</p>

        <h3>
          THIRD<br>
          DUI
        </h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          You're manic, barely sleeping, and making decisions
          faster than you can question them. Alcohol, impulsivity,
          and one more "fuck it" collide. The consequences
          don't disappear just because your judgment was impaired.
        </p>

        <span>FOLLOW THE DECISIONS →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- PRESS SEND -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_press_send_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-purple" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">03 / THE STORY</p>

        <h3>
          PRESS<br>
          SEND.
        </h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          It's 3 AM. You're drunk, emotional, and absolutely
          convinced that someone needs to hear what you
          have to say. You type the message, press send,
          and wake up to words you can't take back.
        </p>

        <span>READ THE RECEIPTS →</span>

      <% end %>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PERSPECTIVES -->
  <section class="bipolar-perspectives-topics"
           id="addiction-perspective-options">

    <div class="bipolar-perspectives-heading">

      <p>01 / PERSPECTIVES ON ADDICTION</p>

      <h2>
        PICK A<br>
        LENS.
      </h2>

      <p class="bipolar-perspectives-subtitle">
        What were you escaping? What were you chasing?
        What were you telling yourself? Each perspective
        examines the same experiences from a different angle:
        craving, judgment, impulses, responsibility, and what
        you can do differently in recovery.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="bipolar-perspectives-grid">

      <!-- BUDDHISM -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_buddhism_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-pink" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">01</p>

        <h3>BUDDHISM</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          You want relief, pleasure, or escape. Buddhism
          examines craving, attachment, and the suffering
          that follows when you mistake a temporary feeling
          for a lasting solution.
        </p>

        <span>EXAMINE THE CRAVING →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- HINDUISM -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_hinduism_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-yellow" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">02</p>

        <h3>HINDUISM</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          Your impulses aren't your entire identity.
          Explore dharma, karma, discernment, and the
          difference between chasing immediate pleasure
          and acting according to your deeper values.
        </p>

        <span>LOOK BEYOND THE IMPULSE →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- STOICISM -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_stoicism_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-purple" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">03</p>

        <h3>STOICISM</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          You can't change what happened. You can examine
          the judgment that preceded the decision, own
          the consequences, and decide what remains
          within your control today.
        </p>

        <span>OWN WHAT'S YOURS →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- CBT -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_cbt_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-black" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">04</p>

        <h3>CBT</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          "One drink won't hurt." "I deserve this."
          "Fuck it, I've already screwed up."
          Identify the distorted thinking, challenge
          the excuses, and check the evidence.
        </p>

        <span>CHECK THE RECEIPTS →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- DBT -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_dbt_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-split" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">05</p>

        <h3>DBT</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          The urge is real. So are the consequences.
          Distress tolerance, emotion regulation,
          and radical acceptance help you survive
          the moment without making it worse.
        </p>

        <span>PAUSE BEFORE YOU ACT →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- IFS -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_ifs_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-pink" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">06</p>

        <h3>IFS</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          One part wants relief. Another wants control.
          Another carries shame. Explore what your
          different parts are trying to protect
          without letting them run the whole show.
        </p>

        <span>MEET YOUR PARTS →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- SHINTO -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_shinto_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-yellow" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">07</p>

        <h3>SHINTO</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          You can't wash away the past. But you can
          acknowledge the damage, repair relationships,
          and rebuild your connection to yourself,
          other people, and the world around you.
        </p>

        <span>BEGIN AGAIN →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- TAOISM -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_taoism_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-purple" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">08</p>

        <h3>TAOISM</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          Stop trying to force every uncomfortable
          feeling to disappear. Explore simplicity,
          restraint, and learning when to act,
          when to wait, and when to let things be.
        </p>

        <span>STOP FORCING IT →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- PAGANISM -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_paganism_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-pink" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">09</p>

        <h3>PAGANISM</h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          Recovery means tending the life you've got.
          Nature, ritual, cycles, and reciprocity offer
          ways to rebuild routines, honor your commitments,
          and take responsibility for what you cultivate.
        </p>

        <span>STAY ROOTED →</span>

      <% end %>


      <!-- THE BIG PICTURE -->
      <%= link_to addiction_perspectives_big_picture_path,
          class: "bipolar-perspective-card bp-card-big-picture" do %>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-number">
          10 / PUTTING IT ALL TOGETHER
        </p>

        <h3>
          THE BIG<br>
          PICTURE
        </h3>

        <p class="bipolar-perspective-description">
          Nine perspectives. Three stories.
          Pain, pleasure, mania, alcohol, impulsivity,
          and consequences. Different ways to understand
          what happened without confusing an explanation
          with an excuse.
        </p>

        <span>PUT IT ALL TOGETHER →</span>

      <% end %>

    </div>

  </section>

</main>
